# Admin feedback & overlays

## Toast after CRUD

After **thêm / sửa / xóa** succeeds, show a Sonner toast. Do not rely only on inline text or silent refetch.

```tsx
import { toast } from "sonner";

toast.success("Đã xóa booking");
toast.success("Đã cập nhật chuyến xe");
```

- Prefer `toast.success` for happy path; use `toast.error` only when there is no inline error UI.
- Keep copy short, Vietnamese, past tense (`Đã …`).

## Never use `window.confirm`

Destructive or irreversible confirms must use an in-app overlay — **not** `window.confirm` / `window.alert`.

Reuse `ConfirmDeleteDialog` (`src/features/ride-admin/components/confirm-delete-dialog.tsx`) or the same responsive pattern for other features.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
if (!window.confirm("Xóa?")) return;

// ✅ GOOD
setDeleting(item); // open ConfirmDeleteDialog
```

## Desktop dialog, mobile bottom sheet

| Viewport | Overlay |
| --- | --- |
| Desktop (`md+`, `useIsDesktop()`) | `Dialog` / `AlertDialog` |
| Mobile (`< md`) | `Sheet` with `side="bottom"` |

Existing helpers:

- **Forms**: `ResponsiveFormShell` + `ResponsiveFormFooter` (`src/components/ui/responsive-form-shell.tsx`)
- **Delete / dangerous confirm**: `ConfirmDeleteDialog` (already switches dialog ↔ bottom sheet)

Do **not** ship mobile UX that only uses a centered modal dialog. New confirm/form overlays must follow the responsive shell pattern (or extend those components).

```tsx
import { useIsDesktop } from "@/hooks/use-media-query";

const isDesktop = useIsDesktop();
// Dialog/AlertDialog when isDesktop; Sheet side="bottom" otherwise
```
